## MILESTONE 4 — Write Actions (Wave 1 — Zero Blast Radius)

### Goal
Enable the first wave of automated remediation actions that produce outputs for human
review but make no configuration changes.

### What to do
1. Set PURESOC_CONNECTOR_RUNNER_ALLOW_PROVIDER_WRITES=true only for the actions below.
   All other write gates remain false.

2. Implement these four ProviderActionTemplates for Microsoft 365:
   a. AUDIT_LOG_EXPORT_SETUP
      - Reads current audit log configuration via Graph API
      - If not enabled: generates a step-by-step setup guide (Markdown) as evidence artifact
      - If already enabled: records a "compliant" evidence artifact
      - No API writes

   b. MFA_COVERAGE_REPORT
      - Queries all admin role members via Graph
      - Checks each for registered MFA methods (authenticationMethods endpoint)
      - Generates a CSV: user, role, mfa_registered (yes/no), mfa_methods
      - Stores CSV as evidence artifact
      - No API writes

   c. GUEST_USER_REVIEW_TASK
      - Queries all guest users (userType eq 'Guest') with last sign-in date
      - Generates a review checklist task for each guest inactive > 90 days
      - Creates ChecklistRun items for the security_operator to action manually
      - No API writes

   d. APP_REGISTRATION_CREDENTIAL_EXPIRY_REPORT
      - Queries all app registrations and their passwordCredentials / keyCredentials
      - Flags any credential expiring within 30 days or already expired
      - Generates a CSV report stored as evidence artifact
      - No API writes

3. Each action must follow the existing action lifecycle:
   preflight → approval (remediation_approver role) → apply → post-snapshot → verify → evidence

4. Surface these four actions in the Recommendations section as "Available Actions" when
   the relevant gaps exist.

5. Update the Approval Queue UI to show action type, preflight results, and a one-click
   Approve button for remediation_approver role.

### Acceptance criteria
- All four actions appear in Recommendations when their corresponding gaps are open
- Each action completes the full lifecycle and produces an evidence artifact
- No Microsoft 365 configuration is modified by any of these actions
- Approval Queue shows pending actions with preflight summary
- remediation_approver can approve; other roles see read-only view

