## MILESTONE 8 — Supplier Assessment Questionnaire

### Goal
Cover NIS2 Article 21(2)(d) supply chain risk management with a lightweight supplier
questionnaire workflow.

### What to do
1. Add Prisma models:
   - Supplier { id, org_id, name, contact_email, website, criticality: low|medium|high|critical,
     status: pending|assessment_sent|responded|reviewed|approved|rejected, created_at }
   - SupplierAssessment { id, supplier_id, org_id, template_version, sent_at, responded_at,
     response_token (unique, hashed), expires_at, status, risk_score }
   - SupplierAnswer { id, assessment_id, question_key, answer_value, evidence_url }

2. Define a standard NIS2 supplier questionnaire with 12 questions covering:
   - Do you have an information security policy? (yes/no/in-progress)
   - Do you conduct annual security awareness training? (yes/no)
   - Do you have a vulnerability management process? (yes/no)
   - Do you perform penetration testing? (never/annually/more_frequent)
   - Do you have a documented incident response plan? (yes/no)
   - Have you had a security incident in the last 12 months? (yes/no/prefer_not_to_say)
   - Do you hold any certifications? (ISO27001/SOC2/NIS2_compliant/none)
   - Do you encrypt data in transit? (yes/no)
   - Do you encrypt data at rest? (yes/no)
   - Do you have a backup and recovery procedure? (yes/no)
   - Do you restrict access on a need-to-know basis? (yes/no)
   - Are you subject to NIS2 yourself? (yes/no/unknown)

3. Risk scoring algorithm (stored as data, not hardcode):
   - Each answer maps to a risk_points value
   - Total score 0–100; <40 = high risk, 40–70 = medium, >70 = low risk

4. Supplier response flow (no login required for suppliers):
   - POST /supplier-assessments/:token/respond — accepts answers, sets responded_at
   - Serve a standalone /supplier-response?token=xxx page (minimal HTML, no auth required)
   - Token is single-use; expires after 30 days
   - After response, send confirmation email to supplier and alert email to org

5. Internal management API:
   - GET  /organizations/:orgId/suppliers
   - POST /organizations/:orgId/suppliers               (create supplier record)
   - POST /organizations/:orgId/suppliers/:id/assess    (send questionnaire email)
   - GET  /organizations/:orgId/suppliers/:id/assessment (view responses + risk score)
   - POST /organizations/:orgId/suppliers/:id/review    (mark as approved/rejected with notes)

6. Supplier Register UI section (under a new "Supply Chain" nav item):
   - Table: Supplier Name | Criticality | Assessment Status | Risk Score | Last Assessed
   - "Add Supplier" button
   - "Send Assessment" button per row
   - Click row → detail panel with all answers and risk score breakdown

7. Map supplier risk to NIS2 supply chain controls in the gap calculation:
   - If org has ≥1 high-criticality supplier not assessed: gap on supply_chain_security control
   - If org has supplier with risk_score < 40: gap on supply_chain_due_diligence control

8. Include supplier register summary in the Evidence Package export.

### Acceptance criteria
- Supplier can respond to questionnaire via public URL with no login
- Risk score is calculated automatically on response submission
- High-risk supplier triggers a compliance gap on the supply chain control
- Supplier register is exportable as CSV
- Assessment link expires after 30 days (responds with 410 Gone after expiry)

