## Cross-Cutting Requirements (apply to all milestones)

### Security
- All new API endpoints require valid session + org membership check
- MSP impersonation must be audit-logged with msp_org_id and target_org_id
- Supplier response tokens must be stored as HMAC-SHA256 hash, never plaintext
- Notification channel destinations (email addresses, webhook URLs) must be org-scoped,
  never cross-org readable
- PDF downloads must be logged in EvidenceAccessLog

### RBAC (use existing roles)
- Notification channel management: org_admin only
- MSP client management: org_admin of the MSP org
- Supplier approve/reject: remediation_approver or compliance_manager
- Supplier add/send-assessment: security_operator or compliance_manager
- Executive summary download: any org member
- Write action approval: remediation_approver only

### Data integrity
- All new Prisma models must have created_at, updated_at timestamps
- All new models with org scope must have org_id foreign key with cascade delete
- Run prisma migrate dev after each milestone's schema changes
- Add appropriate indexes for all foreign keys and frequently filtered columns

### Testing
- Each milestone must include at minimum:
  - One happy-path integration test using the existing test harness
  - One auth boundary test (unauthenticated request returns 401)
  - One role boundary test (wrong role returns 403)
- Use the existing memory persistence mode (PURESOC_PERSISTENCE_MODE=memory) for tests
- Follow existing test file naming and structure conventions

### UI consistency
- Follow existing CSS/component patterns already in the codebase
- New nav items go in the same sidebar/nav structure as existing ones
- All tables follow the existing table component pattern
- All modals follow the existing modal pattern
- No new UI frameworks or component libraries unless one is already present

### Commit discipline
- One commit per milestone, labeled: "feat(milestone-N): <description>"
- Each commit must pass existing tests before proceeding to the next milestone
- Do not mix schema changes from multiple milestones in one migration file

